  "accentSwatches": {
    "note": "The 9 accent options, in display order, as used by the Onboarding theme/color step (Onboarding-1, -3 ... -10) and the Settings > General \"Accent color\" row. Only orange has a named style set (Accent/Main, Bright, Dim, Logo, BG/Accent Bright, BG/Accent Dark); for the other 8 the designer applied the raw hex to the same elements and replaced Dark/BG/Accent Bright (seek-bar fill) with the accent at 24% opacity, except blue at 30% (node 1925:9940 in frame 1902:5245). The selected color-dot ring uses the accent at 30% opacity (verified in frames 1902:4020 ... 1902:6465). Derive Bright/Dim/BG tints for non-orange accents with these rules; record the method in code.",
    "derivationRule": {
      "bgAccentBright": "accent @ alpha 0.24 over the surface; blue uses bgAccentBrightOverrides (orange reference: #D37918@0.24 over #090909 = #39240D vs style #371F06)",
